I see three possible layers now

Layer 1 — immediate / tiny

Make the CDP endpoint configurable instead of hardcoding:

http://127.0.0.1:9222

Then the user can use Edge, Chrome, Opera, etc.

Layer 2 — next

Have QuackSink detect whether a suitable browser/CDP endpoint is available and give the user a much friendlier startup path.

Layer 3 — horizon

QuackSink launches and owns its own browser session.

That last one could eventually eliminate the whole:

"Open browser → start it with magic command-line incantation → THEN start QuackSink"

ritual.

And I don't want Layer 3 contaminating Layer 1.

