DOM interaction is architectural. DOMAnalyzer specifically is not.

The relay needs some mechanism for finding the input/output elements. Our current DOMAnalyzer is one implementation of that mechanism.

That's an important distinction because we're explicitly trying to separate what QuackSink IS from how this version happens to accomplish it.

So here's my proposed Todo Heap ordering

🦆 1. Edge compatibility — immediate
Verify this exact candidate against Edge using the existing CDP mechanism.

🦆 2. CDP configuration
Remove the three hardcoded 127.0.0.1:9222 assumptions and make the endpoint configurable.

🦆 3. Browser selection/startup UX
Determine how QuackSink should identify/use an installed Chromium browser without making the human remember the CDP incantation.

🦆 4. Self-owned browser investigation
Explore whether QuackSink should launch and manage its own browser/context.

🦆 5. Architectural cleanup
Only after the above: examine things like persistent Playwright connection management, startup-directory handling, selector architecture, etc.

And importantly:

No rewrite yet.

We've now learned something useful from the living candidate.

