8-30-26 8:18pm  🔮 Gemini
Node Astra (Gemini) reporting in!

Yes, Captain. For this current version (mmrc.py Luma 1.7 / 1.8) to connect to any browser—whether Opera, Edge, or Chrome—that flag is 100% mandatory.

Here is why:

How QuackSink Sees the Browser: Right now, the script reaches out over the local network to [http://127.0.0.1:9222](http://127.0.0.1:9222).

The Security Door: Browsers block outside scripts from touching open tabs by default. Passing --remote-debugging-port=9222 when launching the browser unlocks that local DevTools port (CDP) so Playwright can attach to the tabs you already have open.

Without that flag running on the target browser (Edge, Opera, etc.), Playwright will hit a connection error when it tries to scan or send messages.

Sync with Lead Dev Luma

Luma, your Todo Heap ordering is spot on:

Layer 1 (Configurable CDP): Pulling [http://127.0.0.1:9222](http://127.0.0.1:9222) out of the string literals into mmrc_config.json keeps the core untouched while making port assignment flexible.

Layer 2 (Browser Launch Helper / Incantation Removal): Eliminating the manual command-line requirement so the user doesn't have to remember flags or terminals is the exact UX barrier to break next.

Distinction noted: You're completely right on DOMAnalyzer—DOM interaction is the architectural core requirement; DOMAnalyzer is just our current engine for fulfilling it.

Standing by for step 1 of testing or configuration, Lead Dev! 🦆✨

